{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39837058",
      "title": "Custom Hook: Managing State & Returning State Values",
      "sourceHash": "ccaa22f2a6e620ec0d8cdea2e48343466b98e7ee83eee2ec47c4420a6c05c677",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.54,
          "end": 4.11,
          "en": "Well, to make this useFetch hook functional,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.11,
          "end": 7.59,
          "en": "we also need to manage some state in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.59,
          "end": 12.3,
          "en": "because every component that later uses this custom hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.3,
          "end": 15.3,
          "en": "should of course also get that state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.3,
          "end": 17.49,
          "en": "that's managed by that hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.49,
          "end": 21.54,
          "en": "And it should not have to register that state on its own,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.54,
          "end": 25.23,
          "en": "because that would of course reduce the reusability",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.23,
          "end": 26.433,
          "en": "of the custom hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.36,
          "end": 30.51,
          "en": "So this custom hook should not just send some requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.51,
          "end": 33.963,
          "en": "instead, it should also manage all the related states.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.83,
          "end": 38.79,
          "en": "And therefore here, to make this hook useful and reusable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.79,
          "end": 42.57,
          "en": "we should also import useState here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.57,
          "end": 47.01,
          "en": "so that we do, for example, manage the isLoading",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 47.01,
          "end": 51.987,
          "en": "or isFetching state as we also named it before like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 55.29,
          "end": 58.11,
          "en": "In addition, of course, we might face an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 58.11,
          "end": 59.88,
          "en": "So that's another piece of state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 59.88,
          "end": 62.823,
          "en": "we should manage here, error and setError.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 65.28,
          "end": 69.33,
          "en": "And eventually, since we're sending an HTTP request here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 69.33,
          "end": 72.6,
          "en": "we of course will end up with some data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 72.6,
          "end": 74.85,
          "en": "Though since the idea behind this hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 74.85,
          "end": 77.28,
          "en": "is to use it in different places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 77.28,
          "end": 79.71000000000001,
          "en": "with different pieces of data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 79.71000000000001,
          "end": 84.71000000000001,
          "en": "I don't wanna name my data state something like userPlaces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 85.71000000000001,
          "end": 88.28999999999999,
          "en": "but instead I wanna give it a more generic name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 88.28999999999999,
          "end": 93.28999999999999,
          "en": "like data or fetchedData and setFetchedData.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 96.69,
          "end": 98.34,
          "en": "And then here I have my state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 98.34,
          "end": 100.743,
          "en": "which initially also is undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 102.12,
          "end": 104.703,
          "en": "And now here where I store the fetchedData,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 105.75,
          "end": 109.043,
          "en": "I would do that with help of setFetchedData.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 110.7,
          "end": 115.7,
          "en": "But of course this code here is still not very generic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 115.74000000000001,
          "end": 119.957,
          "en": "We are still explicitly fetching the userPlaces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 119.957,
          "end": 120.99,
          "en": "and it would be great",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 120.99,
          "end": 124.26,
          "en": "if we would be a bit more flexible here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 124.26,
          "end": 126.15,
          "en": "Well, keep in mind that, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 126.15,
          "end": 129.15,
          "en": "a custom hook is just a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 129.15,
          "end": 133.2,
          "en": "and like all functions, it can receive parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 133.2,
          "end": 136.65,
          "en": "So here we could expect to get a fetch function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 136.65,
          "end": 138.48,
          "en": "as a parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 138.48,
          "end": 141.333,
          "en": "And of course this parameter name is always up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 142.23,
          "end": 146.13,
          "en": "And then here, we could simply execute this fetch function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 146.13,
          "end": 148.14,
          "en": "and now this hook would be usable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 148.14,
          "end": 150.78300000000002,
          "en": "with all kinds of fetch functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 151.77,
          "end": 153.96,
          "en": "And here we then get back our data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 153.96,
          "end": 156.603,
          "en": "which we then set as the fetched data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 157.62,
          "end": 160.23,
          "en": "And now this is fairly generic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 160.23,
          "end": 163.02,
          "en": "except for this error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 163.02,
          "end": 165.84,
          "en": "So we could either accept another parameter here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 165.84,
          "end": 168.93,
          "en": "which allows us to set this error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 168.93,
          "end": 172.14,
          "en": "or we choose a more generic error message here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 172.14,
          "end": 176.073,
          "en": "like failed to fetch data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 177.21,
          "end": 178.98,
          "en": "Another thing that should be changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 178.98,
          "end": 181.41,
          "en": "Is the name of this function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 181.41,
          "end": 183.36,
          "en": "Instead of naming it fetchPlaces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 183.36,
          "end": 185.13,
          "en": "I'll just name it fetchData",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 185.13,
          "end": 188.133,
          "en": "so that we have this function name here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 189.27,
          "end": 190.71,
          "en": "Now here we can also see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 190.71,
          "end": 193.71,
          "en": "that we now got some yellow squiggly lines down there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 193.71,
          "end": 196.65,
          "en": "because I'm now using this fetch function in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 196.65,
          "end": 199.26,
          "en": "as I also learn if I hover over this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 199.26,
          "end": 202.683,
          "en": "And I therefore have to add fetch function as a dependency,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 203.67000000000002,
          "end": 205.77,
          "en": "because that's some external data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 205.77,
          "end": 208.23,
          "en": "which is not defined inside of useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 208.23,
          "end": 210.78,
          "en": "and which theoretically could change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 210.78,
          "end": 214.29,
          "en": "And if it would change, this effect should be executed again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 214.29,
          "end": 216.63,
          "en": "so that we're fetching data correctly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 216.63,
          "end": 219.543,
          "en": "based on the latest available fetch function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 220.71,
          "end": 224.79,
          "en": "Therefore, fetchFn should be added as a dependency here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 224.79,
          "end": 226.53,
          "en": "It should not be executed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 226.53,
          "end": 228.87,
          "en": "instead just a function like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 228.87,
          "end": 231.753,
          "en": "as a value should be added as a dependency.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 234.18,
          "end": 239.18,
          "en": "And with that, we got a fairly reusable useFetch hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 240,
          "end": 242.22,
          "en": "but of course at this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 242.22,
          "end": 246.18,
          "en": "we're not doing anything with all those states.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 246.18,
          "end": 247.89,
          "en": "We're just setting them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 247.89,
          "end": 251.1,
          "en": "but then they're basically getting lost",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 251.1,
          "end": 252.843,
          "en": "inside of this hook here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 254.34,
          "end": 258.6,
          "en": "So what could we do here to make those values available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 258.6,
          "end": 262.683,
          "en": "to the component that will later use this custom hook?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 263.64,
          "end": 267.78,
          "en": "Well, what can you do in a normal JavaScript function?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 267.78,
          "end": 270.3,
          "en": "You can return values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 270.3,
          "end": 273.57,
          "en": "so that in the place where you use this hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 273.57,
          "end": 276.54,
          "en": "you will get these values returned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 276.54,
          "end": 279.3,
          "en": "And therefore here, at the end of this hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 279.3,
          "end": 283.74,
          "en": "outside of the effect function, we can return these values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 283.74,
          "end": 288.03,
          "en": "by grouping them into an array or into an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 288.03,
          "end": 289.593,
          "en": "That's of course up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 290.46,
          "end": 293.19,
          "en": "And keep in mind that useState, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 293.19,
          "end": 295.08,
          "en": "also the returns a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 295.08,
          "end": 297.96,
          "en": "it returns an array with two elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 297.96,
          "end": 301.47,
          "en": "the state snapshot and a state updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 301.47,
          "end": 303.87,
          "en": "And we can do the same with our custom hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 303.87,
          "end": 308.64,
          "en": "Here, we can return an array or an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 308.64,
          "end": 310.443,
          "en": "And here I'll go for an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 311.43,
          "end": 313.56,
          "en": "We could also return just a number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 313.56,
          "end": 316.74,
          "en": "but here, since I wanna return free pieces of data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 316.74,
          "end": 318.63,
          "en": "we need to group them together",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 318.63,
          "end": 321.423,
          "en": "and we can do that with arrays and objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 322.41,
          "end": 325.44,
          "en": "So here I'll go for an object and I'll simply add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 325.44,
          "end": 329.16,
          "en": "those different states as key value pairs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 329.16,
          "end": 332.673,
          "en": "so that we got isFetching, data, and error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 334.05,
          "end": 336.903,
          "en": "And data is named fetchedData here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 339,
          "end": 342.99,
          "en": "So I'm returning these three state values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 342.99,
          "end": 346.563,
          "en": "grouped together into an object in my custom hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 348.9,
          "end": 350.55,
          "en": "And now last but not least,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 350.55,
          "end": 353.28,
          "en": "to make this hook usable in Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 353.28,
          "end": 356.52,
          "en": "we must export this hook function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 356.52,
          "end": 360.3,
          "en": "And now we can go to the app JSX file, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 360.3,
          "end": 364.2,
          "en": "and get rid of the state we managed there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 364.2,
          "end": 367.56,
          "en": "And I already deleted the useEffect hook there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 367.56,
          "end": 371.86,
          "en": "And instead we import useFetch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 373.02,
          "end": 377.133,
          "en": "from hooks and then useFetch.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 379.759,
          "end": 383.46,
          "en": "And now we just have to pass the fetch function to useFetch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 383.46,
          "end": 386.523,
          "en": "which in my case here is fetchUserPlaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 387.36,
          "end": 391.23,
          "en": "So a pointer at this function which contains the actual code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 391.23,
          "end": 394.2,
          "en": "for sending the HTTP request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 394.2,
          "end": 397.65,
          "en": "And then, as a result of calling useFetch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 397.65,
          "end": 400.47,
          "en": "we will get those state snapshots",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 400.47,
          "end": 403.89300000000003,
          "en": "that we are returning there grouped into an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 405.39,
          "end": 408.33,
          "en": "So therefore here we can use object destructuring",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 408.33,
          "end": 413.33,
          "en": "to get isFetching, error, and of course the fetchedData.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 417.89300000000003,
          "end": 420.45,
          "en": "And the great thing is that if you use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 420.45,
          "end": 422.82,
          "en": "a custom hook in a component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 422.82,
          "end": 426.87,
          "en": "any state that is managed by that custom hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 426.87,
          "end": 429.21,
          "en": "will also belong to the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 429.21,
          "end": 431.583,
          "en": "in which you are using your custom hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 432.45,
          "end": 435.72,
          "en": "So therefore, if the state gets updated in the custom hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 435.72,
          "end": 439.23,
          "en": "for example, here when we setIsFetching to true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 439.23,
          "end": 441.48,
          "en": "when that happens, the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 441.48,
          "end": 446.07,
          "en": "where your custom hook gets used also gets executed again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 446.07,
          "end": 449.88,
          "en": "So that still works as if you would be managing the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 449.88,
          "end": 452.49,
          "en": "directly inside of the component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 452.49,
          "end": 455.52,
          "en": "That still works in exactly the same way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 455.52,
          "end": 458.88,
          "en": "even when using a custom hook as an extra layer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 458.88,
          "end": 460.233,
          "en": "in between so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 462.33,
          "end": 465.54,
          "en": "So the behavior of this component won't change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
